stdout ---
Validates json syntax

Usage: jjp check [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --parser <PARSER>
          Parser to use for input

          Possible values:
          - json:      A single json document
          - jsonc:     A single json document with comments and trailing commas
          - jsonlines: One json document per line
          
          [default: json]

      --reporter <REPORTER>
          Format used to report results and errors

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human readable output
          - json:   A single line of json describing the result
          
          [default: pretty]

      --json
          Shorthand for --reporter json

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
	$ echo -en "{\"hello I am valid\": null} " | jjp check

	$ echo -en "{\"coolKey\"}" | jjp check
	error: expected colon after key, found `}`
	 --> stdin:1:11
	  |
	1 | {"coolKey"}
	  |  ---------^
	  |  |
	  |  expected due to `"coolKey"`
	  |
	help: insert colon and placeholder value
	  |
	1 | {"coolKey": "🐟🛹"}
	  |           ++++++++

JSON reporter format:
	$ echo -en "{\"hello I am valid\": null} " | jjp check --json 2>&1 | jjp format
	{ "success": true }

	$ echo -en "{\"coolKey\"}" | jjp check --json 2>&1 | jjp format
	{
	  "success": false,
	  "error": {
	    "kind": "diagnostic",
	    "message": "expected colon after key, found `}`",
	    "file": "stdin",
	    "range": {
	      "start": { "offset": 10, "line": 1, "column": 11 },
	      "end": { "offset": 11, "line": 1, "column": 12 }
	    },
	    "context": [
	      {
	        "message": "expected due to `\"coolKey\"`",
	        "range": {
	          "start": { "offset": 1, "line": 1, "column": 2 },
	          "end": { "offset": 10, "line": 1, "column": 11 }
	        }
	      }
	    ],
	    "fixes": [
	      {
	        "message": "insert colon and placeholder value",
	        "range": {
	          "start": { "offset": 10, "line": 1, "column": 11 },
	          "end": { "offset": 10, "line": 1, "column": 11 }
	        },
	        "replacement": ": \"🐟🛹\""
	      }
	    ]
	  }
	}

